<title>MEXICO: BANCO DE MEXICO TO DRAIN 2.449 BLN PESOS.</title>
<headline>BANCO DE MEXICO TO DRAIN 2.449 BLN PESOS.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 2.449 billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday through a combination of three direct sales of paper and five repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    359 days   20.91 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    180 days   20.85 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     90 days</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    590 million     45 days</p>
<p>    400 million     38 days</p>
<p>    400 million     21 days</p>
<p>    500 million     13 days</p>
<p>    109 million	3 days</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
